meta {
  name: Send Sample (Internal Transfer)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/send
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "destinationBranchId": "{{destinationBranchId}}",
    "logisticsType": "Courier",
    "notes": "Handover at 10:30"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
}

docs {
  Send an ACCEPTED sample to another branch of the tenant (INTERNAL transfer).
  The sample becomes SENT_INTERNAL and a SampleTransfer is created at IN_TRANSIT.

  Refused (422 SAMPLE_SEND_BLOCKED / VALIDATION_ERROR) when:
  - the destination is the sample's own branch;
  - the sample already has an open transfer (in transit, picked up, received, accepted);
  - the report for this test at the sending branch has been worked on (status is not
    PENDING, or it has results, notes, attachments, overall-result entries or
    Notes-section overrides) - a report may only change branch while untouched.

  Group sends pass `force`/`skipInvalid` on the bulk route; a sample that is not
  sendable is skipped when `skipInvalid` is true.
  Internal branch transfer rules (manager flow 2026-09-29):
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER's Technician
    worklist hides its report (list, counts, detail, history, every write, the five
    secondary worklists, attachments, inventory usage, analyser results). It behaves
    as "Lab report not found" (404 LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND) for the sender.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.
}
